<article class="app legal">
  <p class="legal-updated">Last updated 5 October 2026.</p>
  <p>YAVCHN is a free reader for Hacker News and Lobsters at yavchn.com, run by Paul Parks in Singapore. By using it you agree to these terms. The <a href="/privacy" data-win-open="privacy">privacy policy</a> says what YAVCHN keeps about you.</p>

  <h2>What YAVCHN is</h2>
  <p>YAVCHN shows the stories and discussions that Hacker News and Lobsters publish, and readable copies of the articles they link to. It isn't affiliated with either site. The stories and comments belong to those sites and their authors, and the articles belong to their publishers. Voting, commenting and your accounts on those sites all happen on the sites themselves.</p>
  <p>If you publish an article and want YAVCHN to stop showing its readable copy, write to {{ template "legalcontact" }} and it will be removed promptly.</p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p>An account is for one person. You are responsible for what happens through the ways you sign in, so keep your email, GitHub account and passkeys secure. You can delete your account at any time on the Account page.</p>
  <p>Your notes, collections and picture are yours. You let YAVCHN store them and show them to you, and for nothing else. Don't upload a picture that you have no right to use or that is unlawful.</p>

  <h2>Fair use</h2>
  <p>Please don't use YAVCHN in a way that harms it or the sites it reads. That means no attacks on the server, no attempts to get around its limits or into other people's accounts, and no automated use heavy enough to burden YAVCHN, Hacker News, Lobsters or publishers. YAVCHN may limit or close an account that does these things.</p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>YAVCHN is provided as it is, free of charge, and without any warranty. It may be changed, interrupted or shut down at any time, and stories, articles or your data may sometimes be unavailable. Keep your own copy of anything you can't afford to lose; Export your account data on the Account page makes one.</p>
  <p>To the extent the law allows, Paul Parks isn't liable for any loss that comes from using YAVCHN or from being unable to use it.</p>

  <h2>Changes and law</h2>
  <p>These terms may change. If they do, the date at the top changes with it, and continuing to use YAVCHN means you accept the new terms. Singapore law governs these terms.</p>
  <p>Questions about them go to {{ template "legalcontact" }}.</p>
</article>
